  "body": "It's a very common layout / requirement, as shown in these pictures: the entire area of each item is clickable, and there are other links within the area. This layout can be seen on many websites, currently, it takes some tricks to achieve. So, why not just allow `<a>` elements to nest within each other in the standard specification?\r\n\r\n![pic](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8857634/203683276-071b975e-2343-486b-9ab7-9d9deb200264.png)\r\n\r\n![microsoft](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8857634/203473555-2213421a-ec39-4b5d-a542-5d3f680dc9e5.png)\r\n\r\n![apple](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8857634/203473471-59652442-1251-4e1a-8e67-4852092e5858.png)",
